WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.690 --> 00:00:03.620
They're often billed as "family-friendly."

00:00:03.620 --> 00:00:08.590
But sometimes, television shows designed for
young audiences contain some really dark and

00:00:08.590 --> 00:00:09.889
twisted stuff.

00:00:09.889 --> 00:00:14.970
With plots involving depression, abandonment,
and all kinds of real-world horrors, it's

00:00:14.970 --> 00:00:18.430
amazing that some of these episodes ever made
it on the air.

00:00:18.430 --> 00:00:19.780
Here are some of the worst offenders.

00:00:19.780 --> 00:00:23.530
The Fairly Odd Parents - It's a Wishful Life

00:00:23.530 --> 00:00:27.680
From the opening moments of this episode,
things go downhill fast.

00:00:27.680 --> 00:00:33.370
Timmy, the main character, keeps trying to
do good deeds, but nobody appreciates his

00:00:33.370 --> 00:00:35.260
efforts, even his loved ones.

00:00:35.260 --> 00:00:39.460
Understandably upset, he wishes that he'd
never been born — a wish that his fairy

00:00:39.460 --> 00:00:42.379
godparent Wanda reluctantly grants.

00:00:42.379 --> 00:00:47.649
In a parody of It's a Wonderful Life — you
know, the beloved Christmas movie about offing

00:00:47.649 --> 00:00:48.649
yourself...

00:00:48.649 --> 00:00:52.859
"So you still think killing yourself would
make everyone feel happier, right?"

00:00:54.240 --> 00:00:56.559
"Well, I dunno, I guess you're right."

00:00:56.559 --> 00:00:59.079
...Timmy sees what the world would be like
without him.

00:00:59.079 --> 00:01:03.329
However, unlike the movie, Timmy discovers
that everyone he knows is much happier if

00:01:03.329 --> 00:01:04.780
he's not around.

00:01:04.780 --> 00:01:09.120
Even more troubling, Timmy is later shown
the hellish place where all the kids who wished

00:01:09.120 --> 00:01:14.030
they were never born go, implying that this
sort of thing happens on a regular basis.

00:01:14.030 --> 00:01:18.910
Later, Jorgen von Strangle explains that the
whole thing was a setup, aimed at teaching

00:01:18.910 --> 00:01:23.230
a lesson — The lesson that you can't even
trust your fairy godparents, especially if

00:01:23.230 --> 00:01:25.800
you're going through a tough time in your
life.

00:01:25.800 --> 00:01:28.060
Boy Meets World - Cult Fiction

00:01:28.060 --> 00:01:33.261
ABC's coming-of-age sitcom Boy Meets World
didn't shy away from difficult subjects, but

00:01:33.261 --> 00:01:36.840
one episode tops them all: season four's "Cult
Fiction."

00:01:36.840 --> 00:01:41.500
Thanks to his turbulent home life, Shawn frequently
struggles with loneliness and abandonment

00:01:41.500 --> 00:01:46.810
issues, and that makes him a perfect mark
for a local cult that targets troubled kids.

00:01:46.810 --> 00:01:50.580
Before long, he's hopelessly brainwashed by
the cult's leader, Mr. Mack.

00:01:50.580 --> 00:01:55.530
Later, Shawn's teacher Mr. Turner, who served
as a sort of surrogate father to him, is involved

00:01:55.530 --> 00:01:58.270
in a bad motorcycle wreck and is hospitalized.

00:01:58.270 --> 00:02:02.630
Unable to cope with the situation, Shawn brings
Mr. Mack to the hospital with him, where Cory's

00:02:02.630 --> 00:02:05.720
father and Principal Feeny have a confrontation
with the cult leader:

00:02:05.720 --> 00:02:09.410
"Now you brought Shawn down, thanks, now why
don't you just take a hike back to Conland."

00:02:09.410 --> 00:02:12.780
"Now do you see how judgemental these people
are ---"

00:02:12.780 --> 00:02:14.090
"No, no, listen!"

00:02:14.090 --> 00:02:17.780
Meanwhile, Cory and Topanga bring Shawn to
Mr. Turner's room and force him to confront

00:02:17.780 --> 00:02:22.440
the reality of their teacher's condition head-on,
leading to an emotional monologue where Shawn

00:02:22.440 --> 00:02:23.980
talks directly to God:

00:02:23.980 --> 00:02:24.980
"Don't blow me off, John.

00:02:26.440 --> 00:02:28.820
Don't blow me off, God!

00:02:29.780 --> 00:02:33.580
I've never asked you for anything and I never
wanted to come to you like this."

00:02:33.590 --> 00:02:36.190
Rugrats - Angelica's Worst Nightmare

00:02:36.190 --> 00:02:40.480
If you grew up watching Rugrats, you might
not have been aware of the heavy themes.

00:02:40.480 --> 00:02:45.240
But as an adult, you'll soon notice some really
tragic backstories that go unnoticed by the

00:02:45.240 --> 00:02:46.240
babies.

00:02:46.240 --> 00:02:50.140
The darkest episode, though, is "Angelica's
Worst Nightmare."

00:02:50.140 --> 00:02:54.780
Angelica Pickles enjoys her status as a spoiled
only child, so when her mother announces that

00:02:54.780 --> 00:02:59.209
she's pregnant, Angelica's fragile ego is
thrown into a tailspin.

00:02:59.209 --> 00:03:03.170
Her parents ignore her while discussing the
pregnancy, and Angelica begins to worry that

00:03:03.170 --> 00:03:04.750
they won't have time for her.

00:03:04.750 --> 00:03:08.760
In a nightmare, Angelica's baby brother has
arrived, and her parents have forgotten who

00:03:08.760 --> 00:03:13.560
she is, forcing her to live in the laundry
room and eat table scraps.

00:03:13.560 --> 00:03:18.340
After taking everything she loves, the gigantic
baby chases Angelica out of the house before

00:03:18.340 --> 00:03:22.970
catching her and starting to eat the car — which
causes her to wake up, screaming.

00:03:22.970 --> 00:03:26.849
Later, Angelica's parents tell her that they
aren't going to have a baby after all, and

00:03:26.849 --> 00:03:31.990
while she feigns disappointment, Angelica
is secretly pleased about the sad news.

00:03:31.990 --> 00:03:34.630
The Powerpuff Girls - Twisted Sister

00:03:34.630 --> 00:03:39.580
In The Powerpuff Girls episode "Twisted Sister,"
the trio of cute cartoon superheroes find

00:03:39.580 --> 00:03:44.170
themselves overwhelmed with school, chores,
and constantly saving the day.

00:03:44.170 --> 00:03:47.489
They decide to create a fourth Powerpuff Girl
to help share the load.

00:03:47.489 --> 00:03:51.740
But instead of following the Professor's original
formula of sugar, spice, and everything nice,

00:03:51.740 --> 00:03:56.310
the girls use artificial sweetener, dirt,
and things like crayons, lizards, and boxing

00:03:56.310 --> 00:03:59.879
gloves — along with the secret ingredient,
Chemical X.

00:03:59.879 --> 00:04:04.980
The result is a gigantic, misshapen, and not
very bright new Powerpuff Girl that they name

00:04:04.980 --> 00:04:05.840
Bunny.

00:04:14.800 --> 00:04:19.299
Unfortunately, Bunny mixes things up — throwing
police officers in jail while letting the

00:04:19.299 --> 00:04:20.530
criminals run free.

00:04:20.530 --> 00:04:25.460
When her sisters arrive, they angrily tell
Bunny that she's bad and can't be a Powerpuff

00:04:25.460 --> 00:04:26.460
Girl.

00:04:26.460 --> 00:04:30.590
Heartbroken, Bunny flies away to sob her heart
out on a lonely cliffside, but returns when

00:04:30.590 --> 00:04:35.440
her sisters are in danger to defeat all the
bad guys, excited that she's finally been

00:04:35.440 --> 00:04:36.440
"good."

00:04:36.440 --> 00:04:41.650
Unfortunately, this effort was too much for
Bunny's unstable body, and she explodes.

00:04:41.650 --> 00:04:45.970
A piece of her dress flutters to the ground,
and the girls cry as they realize how awful

00:04:45.970 --> 00:04:47.020
they were.

00:04:47.020 --> 00:04:50.470
Even the narrator of the show can barely handle
it.

00:04:50.470 --> 00:04:55.410
"It's so sad, I can't take it."

00:04:55.410 --> 00:04:57.770
Tom &amp; Jerry - Blue Cat Blues

00:04:57.770 --> 00:05:03.250
In stark contrast to the typical slapstick
antics found in the classic cartoon Tom &amp; Jerry,

00:05:03.250 --> 00:05:09.530
the 1956 feature "Blue Cat Blues" has an extremely
tragic — and traumatizing — plot.

00:05:09.530 --> 00:05:11.460
Tom falls in love with a beautiful white cat.

00:05:11.460 --> 00:05:15.810
But although she returns his affections at
first, she eventually leaves Tom for a rich

00:05:15.810 --> 00:05:17.620
neighborhood cat named Butch.

00:05:17.620 --> 00:05:22.840
Jerry tells Tom to move on with his life,
but Tom can't let go, and eventually literally

00:05:22.840 --> 00:05:26.150
sells himself into slavery to buy her a car:

00:05:26.150 --> 00:05:34.419
"It cost him an arm and a leg, but he willingly
sold himself into slavery… for love."

00:05:34.419 --> 00:05:37.699
— which promptly gets destroyed by Butch's
fancy coupe.

00:05:37.699 --> 00:05:42.229
Heartbroken and hopelessly in debt, Tom turns
to the bottle — the milk bottle, that is

00:05:42.229 --> 00:05:47.750
— and decides to sit down on the train tracks
and end it all once the two cats get married.

00:05:47.750 --> 00:05:52.960
Jerry, at a loss on how to cheer up his friend,
consoles himself that at least his own girlfriend

00:05:52.960 --> 00:05:54.740
wouldn't do that to him.

00:05:54.740 --> 00:05:59.650
Just then, Jerry sees his own girlfriend drive
by with a different mouse, with a "Just Married"

00:05:59.650 --> 00:06:02.080
sign on the back of their car, too.

00:06:02.080 --> 00:06:06.430
Realizing that life now holds nothing for
him either, Jerry joins Tom on the track,

00:06:06.430 --> 00:06:10.540
and the screen fades to black as the sound
of a train whistle approaches.

00:06:10.540 --> 00:06:11.620
The end.

00:06:11.620 --> 00:06:14.620
Thomas the Tank Engine (The Sad Story of Henry)

00:06:14.620 --> 00:06:19.190
Most episodes of the popular children's series
Thomas the Tank Engine are rather cheerful

00:06:19.190 --> 00:06:23.400
affairs, usually with Thomas or one of the
other engines learning a valuable lesson after

00:06:23.400 --> 00:06:25.919
being stubborn or childish in some way.

00:06:25.919 --> 00:06:30.710
In "The Sad Story of Henry," a similar setup
leads to a decidedly dark turn.

00:06:30.710 --> 00:06:35.190
The green engine Henry is afraid the rain
will ruin his bright and shiny paint, so he

00:06:35.190 --> 00:06:40.600
takes refuge inside a tunnel, and then refuses
to leave it, even after the rain stops.

00:06:40.600 --> 00:06:45.610
When logical reasoning, firm orders, and even
brute force fail to budge the silly steam

00:06:45.610 --> 00:06:49.740
engine, railway manager and father figure
Sir Topham Hatt finally gives up.

00:06:49.740 --> 00:06:53.990
Workers pull up the rails to the tunnel and
lay bricks over the entrance, trapping Henry

00:06:53.990 --> 00:06:54.990
inside.

00:06:54.990 --> 00:06:59.370
The other engines cheekily whistle at Henry
as they pass, and he becomes extremely lonely

00:06:59.370 --> 00:07:03.229
and miserable, and the soot from their smoke
ruins his shiny paint.

00:07:03.229 --> 00:07:08.419
As the sad green engine contemplates his unknown
fate, even the narrator, Ringo Starr, gets

00:07:08.419 --> 00:07:10.300
in on Henry's public humiliation.

00:07:10.300 --> 00:07:14.600
"But I think he deserved his punishment…
don't you?"

00:07:14.600 --> 00:07:19.160
That's right, kids: if you misbehave, then
it's completely normal for your parents to

00:07:19.160 --> 00:07:21.949
lock you in your room and not let you out.

00:07:21.949 --> 00:07:25.240
And if you've been really naughty, they might
never come back.

00:07:25.240 --> 00:07:28.460
And then a former Beatle will say you deserved
everything you got.

00:07:28.460 --> 00:07:29.509
Thanks for watching!

00:07:29.509 --> 00:07:32.100
Click the Looper icon to subscribe to our
YouTube channel.

00:07:32.100 --> 00:07:34.690
Plus check out all this other cool stuff we
know you'll love too.

